.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/pify Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "pify [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/pify.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/pify)"
.PP
.RS 4
Promisify a callback-style function 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install \-\-save pify
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const fs = require('fs');
const pify = require('pify');

// promisify a single function

pify(fs\&.readFile)('package\&.json', 'utf8')\&.then(data => {
    console\&.log(JSON\&.parse(data)\&.name);
    //=> 'pify'
});

// or promisify all methods in a module

pify(fs)\&.readFile('package\&.json', 'utf8')\&.then(data => {
    console\&.log(JSON\&.parse(data)\&.name);
    //=> 'pify'
});
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "pify(input, [promiseModule], [options])"
Returns a promise wrapped version of the supplied function or module\&.
.SS "input"
Type: \fRfunction\fP, \fRobject\fP

.PP
Callback-style function or module whose methods you want to promisify\&.
.SS "promiseModule"
Type: \fRfunction\fP

.PP
Custom promise module to use instead of the native one\&.

.PP
Check out \fR\fRpinkie-promise\fP\fP if you need a tiny promise polyfill\&.
.SS "options"
.SS "multiArgs"
Type: \fRboolean\fP 
.br
 Default: \fRfalse\fP

.PP
By default, the promisified function will only return the second argument from the callback, which works fine for most APIs\&. This option can be useful for modules like \fRrequest\fP that return multiple arguments\&. Turning this on will make it return an array of all arguments from the callback, excluding the error argument, instead of just the second argument\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const request = require('request');
const pify = require('pify');

pify(request, {multiArgs: true})('https://sindresorhus\&.com')\&.then(result => {
    const [httpResponse, body] = result;
});
.fi
.PP
.SS "include"
Type: \fRarray\fP of (\fRstring\fP|\fRregex\fP)

.PP
Methods in a module to promisify\&. Remaining methods will be left untouched\&.
.SS "exclude"
Type: \fRarray\fP of (\fRstring\fP|\fRregex\fP) 
.br
 Default: \fR[/\&.+Sync$/]\fP

.PP
Methods in a module \fBnot\fP to promisify\&. Methods with names ending with \fR'Sync'\fP are excluded by default\&.
.SS "excludeMain"
Type: \fRboolean\fP 
.br
 Default: \fRfalse\fP

.PP
By default, if given module is a function itself, this function will be promisified\&. Turn this option on if you want to promisify only methods of the module\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const pify = require('pify');

function fn() {
    return true;
}

fn\&.method = (data, callback) => {
    setImmediate(() => {
        callback(data, null);
    });
};

// promisify methods but not fn()
const promiseFn = pify(fn, {excludeMain: true});

if (promiseFn()) {
    promiseFn\&.method('hi')\&.then(data => {
        console\&.log(data);
    });
}
.fi
